      <description><![CDATA[<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,system-ui;line-height:1.45;color:#1d1d1f}h4{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:#6e6e73;margin:14px 0 4px}ul{padding-left:18px;margin:0}li{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}h4{color:#a1a1a6}}</style><h4>Highlights</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Your app icon on the store page.</strong> In <strong>Preview the store page</strong>, click the icon (or drop a picture on it) to use your app&#39;s own: one of your pictures, or a file. It&#39;s kept with the design, so each app keeps its own. Until you choose one, an app icon already on the design is used, else the app&#39;s initial.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Fixes</h4>
<ul>
<li>The Illustrations in the Images panel fit the panel again: wide ones no longer push the grid past its edge or over Badges.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
